1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,067
An apron.

2
00:00:01,417 --> 00:00:02,398
A hangar.

3
00:00:02,748 --> 00:00:04,519
Two inspection drones.

4
00:00:04,869 --> 00:00:06,639
An aircraft taxiing.

5
00:00:06,989 --> 00:00:09,379
One drone slips behind the hangar.

6
00:00:09,729 --> 00:00:11,307
What should the screen say?

7
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,506
MoVi gives every tracked object one of
three answers.

8
00:00:16,856 --> 00:00:17,901
I see it.

9
00:00:18,251 --> 00:00:20,790
I don't see it: here is where it can be.

10
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:22,462
Or: I don't know.

11
00:00:22,812 --> 00:00:26,908
What it has not observed, it marks
unverified, never empty.

12
00:00:27,258 --> 00:00:31,482
A possible-presence warning stays on until
a sensor looks again.

13
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:39,703
Radar, LiDAR, visible and thermal cameras,
and what aircraft and drones broadcast.

14
00:00:40,053 --> 00:00:42,762
All simulated from public data sheets.

15
00:00:43,112 --> 00:00:46,611
Each sensor has blind spots, and MoVi
draws them.

16
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,649
Fog, then heavy rain.

17
00:00:51,999 --> 00:00:56,815
By calculation, the cameras' reach
collapses, and MoVi declares it, per

18
00:00:56,815 --> 00:00:57,290
sensor.

19
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,669
Only the radar is left: no redundancy.

20
00:01:01,019 --> 00:01:06,428
If the radar also fails, a fault we
inject, reliability is lost: warnings

21
00:01:06,428 --> 00:01:07,910
would come too late.

22
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:12,863
Two drones fly close.

23
00:01:13,213 --> 00:01:16,157
Too close to separate: unresolved tracks.

24
00:01:16,507 --> 00:01:18,725
Event: contact, inferred.

25
00:01:19,075 --> 00:01:23,086
A possible-debris volume opens, and never
shrinks on its own.

26
00:01:23,436 --> 00:01:29,726
Our weak point: in simulation, contact was
declared within two seconds in one run out

27
00:01:29,726 --> 00:01:30,540
of sixteen.

28
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:36,143
An engine fails during taxi, with a flash.

29
00:01:36,493 --> 00:01:42,464
The flash blinds the cameras: MoVi marks
them unreliable, in thirty-two runs out of

30
00:01:42,464 --> 00:01:43,255
thirty-two.

31
00:01:43,605 --> 00:01:47,019
In the model, the radar alone still sees
the aircraft.

32
00:01:47,369 --> 00:01:49,694
Behind the smoke: not observed.

33
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,265
First, the limits.

34
00:01:54,615 --> 00:01:57,858
Everything is simulated from public data
sheets.

35
00:01:58,208 --> 00:02:00,917
Almost half the values are assumed.

36
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:02,867
No physical sensor.

37
00:02:03,217 --> 00:02:05,479
Classes are labelled by hand.

38
00:02:05,829 --> 00:02:08,879
Event rules are not yet in the prototype.

39
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:12,813
For aircraft in flight, warnings are not
yet in time.

40
00:02:13,163 --> 00:02:15,211
Total delay: not measured.

41
00:02:15,561 --> 00:02:21,422
What holds, in simulation: a drone hidden
behind a building was announced in time in

42
00:02:21,422 --> 00:02:24,073
two hundred passes out of two hundred.

43
00:02:24,423 --> 00:02:28,071
Zero passes out of six hundred lost that
warning.

44
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:34,457
The core comes from our short-range
version: a person behind an obstacle, a

45
00:02:34,457 --> 00:02:36,952
depth camera, the same three answers.

46
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,475
MoVi.

47
00:02:40,825 --> 00:02:44,366
Seen, not seen, unknown: declared for
every track.

48
00:02:44,716 --> 00:02:46,786
It observes and warns.

49
00:02:47,136 --> 00:02:49,269
No output is a command.

50
00:02:49,619 --> 00:02:51,902
A project by SDMs.
